{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/976266-triat-the-universe-and-werewolf-the-apocalypse-in-the-future-and-beyond","id":976266,"title":"Triat, the Universe, and Werewolf the Apocalypse in the Future and beyond!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T19:35:46-07:00","id":976266,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Triat, the Universe, and Werewolf the Apocalypse in the Future and beyond!","content":"So the game I most wanted to explore for a chronicle set in the future like say a space opera setting like Outlaw Star/Trigun/Cowboy Bebop is Werewolf. So I was thinking about the cosmology in a more cosmic context. Instead of the Universe revolving around what happens around the Earth and sharing its fate, what if the Triat are Universal constants but their context is defined by microcosms revolving around Celestines such as Gaia. So for instance the sanity of the Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld is defined by the history of life around the Gaian Sphere, farther away from from it perhaps context starts to null and until the spiritual gravity around another Mothergod again defines a unique corner of the Universe. So maybe for instance the Red Star Anthelios, the Eye of the Wyrm represents another Gaea that underwent an Apocalypse. Maybe in other Worlds the Weaver Succeed, Coughborgcough, with swirling Nebula filled with Anomolies representing the Wyld, or even hyperspace or some such impossible dimension belonging to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> This blends well with the Mokole History were the Apocalypse exists in Cycles. It also fits well with say Chulorviah and Inquisitors. Maybe Chulorviah are from other Corners of the Universe lost to their local Wyrm. The Inquisitors could also be from another worlds Wyrm, maybe even another Worlds equivalent to Pentex sizing up this edge of the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> This Universal Paradigm makes the Apocalypse still gravely important, but also one fight among many. It provides a backdrop to bring back Earth after the Apocalypse as well as perhaps save the Seeds of Gaia elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:51:39-07:00","id":976282,"title":"","content":"I would suggest there be a Galactic Gaia and a Galactic Triat (Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm), each with aspects that are localized to specific star systems, with a spiritual quarantine isolating any star system that is corrupted enough to potentially trigger an Apocalypse. The Sol System could have suffered an Apocalypse, but something could have created a generation ship that escaped the spiritual quarantine (or a sleeper ship that slept through the Apocalypse). Human civilization would be derived from the hundreds of millions of survivors, with Changelings and Fera being among the survivors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T21:17:42-07:00","id":976342,"title":"","content":"That is kind of what I was going with, more or less. Only the Mightiest/most enlightened of the Avatars knowing about their fellows outside their System. So Sea or another Celestine aspect of Gaia would know/sense greater parts of the Universe. With things like Maeljin and even Number Two ignorant of Hate and Corruption outside the human sphere. This explains why beings such as alien star spirits are Alien, they know things from traveling through seldom trod space. Incarna aspects of planets such as Katanka Sonnak only know whispers of Universe, but Celestines know greater understandings, hence why Helios was tricked by a Mirror displaying another Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:53:11-07:00","id":976518,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it would only be the Supernals (Gaia-Balance, Weaver-Order, Wyld-Chaos, and Wyrm-Entropy) that would know the truth of the matter (if they were sane enough to think about it). Now, the only question is whether the Space Garou are the last survivors of the Apocalypse or the exiles from a Technocratic Distophia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}